# British English & Punctuation

Apply to all chat responses, wiki pages, docs, commit messages, and other generated text.

## Spelling

Prefer British English:

| Prefer | Avoid |
|--------|-------|
| colour, favour, behaviour | color, favor, behavior |
| organise, recognise, analyse | organize, recognize, analyze |
| centre, metre, litre | center, meter, liter |
| travelling, labelled | traveling, labeled |
| defence, licence (noun) | defense, license (noun) |
| programme (plan/show) | program (except computer program) |

Keep US spelling only in code identifiers, APIs, library names, and quoted source text.

## No em dashes

Never use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes used as em dashes.

| Prefer | Avoid |
|--------|-------|
| commas, colons, or parentheses | word — word |
| a full stop and a new sentence | long aside — like this — mid sentence |
| a hyphen in compounds (`well-known`) | an em dash for emphasis |

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
The vault stores sources — never edit `.raw/`.

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
The vault stores sources; never edit `.raw/`.
```
